    "## Q1. Explain the difference between simple linear regression and multiple linear regression. Provide an example of each."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Answer:**\n",
    "\n",
    "**Simple Linear Regression:** Uses one independent variable to predict a dependent variable.\n",
    "- Formula: y = β₀ + β₁x + ε\n",
    "\n",
    "**Multiple Linear Regression:** Uses two or more independent variables to predict a dependent variable.\n",
    "- Formula: y = β₀ + β₁x₁ + β₂x₂ + ... + βₙxₙ + ε\n",
    "\n",
    "**Examples:**\n",
    "- Simple: Predicting house price based only on square footage\n",
    "- Multiple: Predicting house price based on square footage, number of bedrooms, location, and age"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Q2. Discuss the assumptions of linear regression. How can you check whether these assumptions hold in a given dataset?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Answer:**\n",
    "\n",
    "**Key Assumptions:**\n",
    "1. **Linearity:** Relationship between X and Y is linear\n",
    "2. **Independence:** Observations are independent\n",
    "3. **Homoscedasticity:** Constant variance of residuals\n",
    "4. **Normality:** Residuals are normally distributed\n",
    "5. **No multicollinearity** (for multiple regression)\n",
    "\n",
    "**How to check:**\n",
    "- **Linearity:** Scatter plots, residual vs fitted plots\n",
    "- **Independence:** Durbin-Watson test\n",
    "- **Homoscedasticity:** Residual vs fitted plot, Breusch-Pagan test\n",
    "- **Normality:** Q-Q plot, Shapiro-Wilk test, histogram of residuals\n",
    "- **Multicollinearity:** Variance Inflation Factor (VIF)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Example: Checking assumptions with code\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "from scipy import stats\n",
    "import statsmodels.api as sm\n",
    "\n",
    "# Generate sample data\n",
    "np.random.seed(42)\n",
    "X = np.random.randn(100, 1)\n",
    "y = 2 * X.flatten() + np.random.randn(100) * 0.5\n",
    "\n",
    "# Fit linear regression\n",
    "X_with_const = sm.add_constant(X)\n",
    "model = sm.OLS(y, X_with_const).fit()\n",
    "residuals = model.resid\n",
    "fitted = model.fittedvalues\n",
    "\n",
    "# Check assumptions visually\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(2, 2, figsize=(12, 10))\n",
    "\n",
    "# 1. Linearity & Homoscedasticity\n",
    "axes[0, 0].scatter(fitted, residuals)\n",
    "axes[0, 0].axhline(y=0, color='r', linestyle='--')\n",
    "axes[0, 0].set_xlabel('Fitted Values')\n",
    "axes[0, 0].set_ylabel('Residuals')\n",
    "axes[0, 0].set_title('Residuals vs Fitted')\n",
    "\n",
    "# 2. Normality (Q-Q plot)\n",
    "stats.probplot(residuals, dist=\"norm\", plot=axes[0, 1])\n",
    "axes[0, 1].set_title('Q-Q Plot')\n",
    "\n",
    "# 3. Histogram of residuals\n",
    "axes[1, 0].hist(residuals, bins=20, edgecolor='black')\n",
    "axes[1, 0].set_xlabel('Residuals')\n",
    "axes[1, 0].set_ylabel('Frequency')\n",
    "axes[1, 0].set_title('Histogram of Residuals')\n",
    "\n",
    "# 4. Scale-Location plot\n",
    "axes[1, 1].scatter(fitted, np.sqrt(np.abs(residuals)))\n",
    "axes[1, 1].set_xlabel('Fitted Values')\n",
    "axes[1, 1].set_ylabel('√|Residuals|')\n",
    "axes[1, 1].set_title('Scale-Location Plot')\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Statistical tests\n",
    "shapiro_stat, shapiro_p = stats.shapiro(residuals)\n",
    "print(f\"Shapiro-Wilk test p-value: {shapiro_p:.4f}\")\n",
    "print(\"Residuals are normally distributed\" if shapiro_p > 0.05 else \"Residuals may not be normally distributed\")"
   ]
  },
  {
