   "source": [
    "## Q4. Explain the concept of gradient descent. How is it used in machine learning?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Answer:**\n",
    "\n",
    "**Gradient Descent** is an optimization algorithm that iteratively adjusts parameters to minimize a cost function.\n",
    "\n",
    "**How it works:**\n",
    "1. Start with random parameter values\n",
    "2. Calculate the gradient (slope) of the cost function\n",
    "3. Update parameters in the opposite direction of the gradient\n",
    "4. Repeat until convergence\n",
    "\n",
    "**Update rule:** θ = θ - α ∇J(θ)\n",
    "- θ: parameters\n",
    "- α: learning rate\n",
    "- ∇J(θ): gradient of cost function\n",
    "\n",
    "**Use in Machine Learning:**\n",
    "- Training neural networks (backpropagation)\n",
    "- Linear and logistic regression\n",
    "- Support Vector Machines\n",
    "- Deep learning models"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Example: Gradient Descent implementation for linear regression\n",
    "def gradient_descent(X, y, learning_rate=0.01, epochs=1000):\n",
    "    m = len(y)\n",
    "    theta_0 = 0  # intercept\n",
    "    theta_1 = 0  # slope\n",
    "    \n",
    "    for epoch in range(epochs):\n",
    "        # Predictions\n",
    "        y_pred = theta_0 + theta_1 * X\n",
    "        \n",
    "        # Calculate gradients\n",
    "        grad_0 = (1/m) * np.sum(y_pred - y)\n",
    "        grad_1 = (1/m) * np.sum((y_pred - y) * X)\n",
    "        \n",
    "        # Update parameters\n",
    "        theta_0 -= learning_rate * grad_0\n",
    "        theta_1 -= learning_rate * grad_1\n",
    "        \n",
    "        # Print progress\n",
    "        if epoch % 200 == 0:\n",
    "            cost = (1/(2*m)) * np.sum((y_pred - y)**2)\n",
    "            print(f\"Epoch {epoch}: θ₀={theta_0:.4f}, θ₁={theta_1:.4f}, Cost={cost:.4f}\")\n",
    "    \n",
    "    return theta_0, theta_1\n",
    "\n",
    "# Sample data\n",
    "X = np.array([1, 2, 3, 4, 5])\n",
    "y = np.array([2, 4, 6, 8, 10])\n",
    "\n",
    "# Run gradient descent\n",
    "print(\"Running Gradient Descent:\")\n",
    "theta_0, theta_1 = gradient_descent(X, y, learning_rate=0.01, epochs=1000)\n",
    "print(f\"\\nFinal parameters: θ₀={theta_0:.4f}, θ₁={theta_1:.4f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Expected: θ₀=0, θ₁=2\")"
   ]
  },
