   "source": [
    "## Q7. Describe the polynomial regression model. How is it different from linear regression?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Answer:**\n",
    "\n",
    "**Polynomial Regression:** Extends linear regression by adding polynomial terms of the independent variable(s).\n",
    "\n",
    "**Formula (degree 2):** y = β₀ + β₁x + β₂x² + ε\n",
    "\n",
    "**Key differences from Linear Regression:**\n",
    "\n",
    "| Aspect | Linear Regression | Polynomial Regression |\n",
    "|--------|------------------|----------------------|\n",
    "| Relationship | Linear | Curvilinear |\n",
    "| Model flexibility | Low | High |\n",
    "| Equation form | y = β₀ + β₁x | y = β₀ + β₁x + β₂x² + ... |\n",
    "| Overfitting risk | Low | High |\n",
    "| Interpretability | Simple | Complex |\n",
    "\n",
    "**Note:** Polynomial regression is still linear in parameters (coefficients), but nonlinear in features."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Example: Linear vs Polynomial Regression\n",
    "from sklearn.preprocessing import PolynomialFeatures\n",
    "from sklearn.pipeline import make_pipeline\n",
    "\n",
    "# Generate nonlinear data\n",
    "np.random.seed(42)\n",
    "X = np.sort(5 * np.random.rand(80, 1), axis=0)\n",
    "y = np.sin(X).ravel() + np.random.randn(80) * 0.1\n",
    "\n",
    "# Create models\n",
    "linear_model = LinearRegression()\n",
    "poly_model = make_pipeline(PolynomialFeatures(degree=4), LinearRegression())\n",
    "\n",
    "# Fit models\n",
    "linear_model.fit(X, y)\n",
    "poly_model.fit(X, y)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Predictions\n",
    "X_test = np.linspace(0, 5, 100).reshape(-1, 1)\n",
    "y_linear_pred = linear_model.predict(X_test)\n",
    "y_poly_pred = poly_model.predict(X_test)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Visualization\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(10, 6))\n",
    "plt.scatter(X, y, color='blue', alpha=0.5, label='Data')\n",
    "plt.plot(X_test, y_linear_pred, color='red', label='Linear Regression', linewidth=2)\n",
    "plt.plot(X_test, y_poly_pred, color='green', label='Polynomial Regression (deg=4)', linewidth=2)\n",
    "plt.xlabel('X')\n",
    "plt.ylabel('y')\n",
    "plt.title('Linear vs Polynomial Regression')\n",
    "plt.legend()\n",
    "plt.grid(True, alpha=0.3)\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Compare R² scores\n",
    "print(f\"Linear Regression R²: {linear_model.score(X, y):.4f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Polynomial Regression R²: {poly_model.score(X, y):.4f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
